What actually matters is charge-cycle count and pass-through behavior — whether the bank can charge your laptop and itself at the same time without shutting off. We test both before anything ships, and we publish the real numbers, not the theoretical ones.', 'Battery capacity claims are inflated industry-wide. Here''s how to read the number that actually matters.', '/demo/hero/demo-electronics.svg', NULL, NULL, 'published', '2026-07-05T13:31:35.435Z', NULL, ARRAY['power', 'charging', 'battery'], 'Product Notes', 217, '2026-08-12T13:31:35.259Z', '2026-08-12T13:31:35.259Z');

A hub that consolidates cables, a lamp with a charging port built in, and a mouse shaped for an actual hand beat almost anything with a screen or an app. The theme is: solve one annoyance completely, and disappear into the desk.

The full list, with why each one earns its spot, is worth five minutes if your desk currently looks like a cable drawer exploded on it.', 'Most desk gadgets end up in a drawer within a month. These five earn a permanent spot.', '/demo/hero/demo-electronics.svg', NULL, NULL, 'published', '2026-07-19T13:31:35.434Z', NULL, ARRAY['desk', 'workspace', 'guide'], 'Buying Guides', 230, '2026-08-12T13:31:35.259Z', '2026-08-12T13:31:35.259Z');

Aviator is tuned close to flat, which means vocals sit where they were mixed instead of getting buried under bass that was never supposed to be that loud. It''s a less flattering demo and a better six-hour listen, which is the actual use case for a pair of headphones you''re buying to wear at a desk.

If you genuinely want more bass, the companion app has an EQ preset for that. We just don''t think it should be the default.', 'Most headphones in this price range boost the bass because it sells better in a five-second store demo. Here''s why we didn''t.', '/demo/hero/demo-electronics.svg', NULL, NULL, 'published', '2026-08-02T13:31:35.432Z', NULL, ARRAY['headphones', 'audio', 'engineering'], 'Product Notes', 310, '2026-08-12T13:31:35.259Z', '2026-08-12T13:31:35.259Z');

It''s also a renewable, biodegradable crop-based wax rather than a petroleum byproduct, which matters to us even though it doesn''t show up anywhere on the label. The jars are reusable once the wax is gone — we''ve had customers turn them into pen cups for years.', 'Paraffin burns hotter and throws scent faster. We use soy anyway, for reasons that show up months later, not on day one.', '/demo/hero/artisan-craft.svg', NULL, NULL, 'published', '2026-07-05T13:31:35.635Z', NULL, ARRAY['candles', 'materials'], 'Behind the Work', 281, '2026-08-12T13:31:35.259Z', '2026-08-12T13:31:35.259Z');

Avoid extreme temperature swings — don''t pour boiling water into a mug straight from the fridge. Stoneware can handle heat, but thermal shock is still thermal shock.

If a glaze ever develops a hairline crack, it''s almost always cosmetic (a ''crazing'' pattern in the glaze layer, not the clay body underneath) and doesn''t affect food safety. If you''re ever unsure, email us a photo.', 'Stoneware is tougher than it looks, but a few habits will double the life of anything glazed by hand.', '/demo/hero/artisan-craft.svg', NULL, NULL, 'published', '2026-07-19T13:31:35.634Z', NULL, ARRAY['ceramics', 'care'], 'Care Guides', 316, '2026-08-12T13:31:35.259Z', '2026-08-12T13:31:35.259Z');

The greenware dries for a week before a first bisque fire, gets glazed by hand — dipped, not sprayed — and goes back in for a second firing at cone 6. That''s roughly two weeks from wet clay to a mug that can go in a dishwasher.

We could speed this up with slip casting and a mold. We haven''t, because a mold mug and a thrown mug don''t feel the same in your hand, and that difference is the entire point of buying from a studio instead of a catalog.', 'From a lump of stoneware to a glazed mug is about a two-week process, most of it waiting on a kiln.', '/demo/hero/artisan-craft.svg', NULL, NULL, 'published', '2026-08-02T13:31:35.633Z', NULL, ARRAY['pottery', 'process', 'studio'], 'Behind the Work', 75, '2026-08-12T13:31:35.259Z', '2026-08-12T13:31:35.259Z');

